    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d209">

                <pb facs="0198" n="124" sameAs="frus:frus1865p2/pg124"/>

                <head>Mr. Burnley to Mr.
                        Hunter</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-04-18"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 18, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> With reference to Mr. Seward’s note of the
                    6th ultimo, asking for the extradition of Vernon G. Locke, I have the honor to
                    enclose copy of a despatch which I have received from his excellency the
                    governor of the Bahamas in reply to my despatch communicating to him copy of the
                    above-mentioned note.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with high consideration, sir, your most obedient, humble
                    servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. HUME BURNLEY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Hunter,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d209-a1.xml" xpointer="d209-a1"/>
